.TH DIODON-TASKSHEET 1 "2026" "diodon-tasksheet 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diodon-tasksheet \- control the Tasksheet plugin of the Diodon clipboard manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diodon-tasksheet
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Tasksheet plugin adds a personal list of words and notes next to
Diodon's clipboard history. Items can be moved from the clipboard to the
tasksheet with a button or by drag and drop. Tasks are stored in
.IR ~/.local/share/diodon/tasksheet.ini .
.PP
.B diodon-tasksheet
talks to the plugin inside the running Diodon, so it is meant to be bound
to keyboard shortcuts.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tasksheet
Open the Tasksheet tab, or close the popup if that tab is already showing.
This is the default.
.TP
.B clipboard
Open the Clipboard tab, or close the popup if that tab is already showing.
.TP
.B enable
Add the plugin to the list of plugins Diodon loads for the current user.
Restart Diodon afterwards.
.TP
.B disable
Remove the plugin from that list.
.TP
.BR hotkeys " [" \-\-undo ]
Set up the GNOME keyboard shortcuts Super+V (Clipboard tab) and Super+Y
(Tasksheet tab). Other shortcuts that already use these keys are released
first and restored by
.BR \-\-undo .
On other desktops, create two custom shortcuts that run
.B diodon-tasksheet clipboard
and
.BR "diodon-tasksheet tasksheet" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/diodon/tasksheet.ini
The saved tasks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if Diodon or its plugin cannot be reached, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR diodon (1)
